1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,760
I first met The Roots in 2004 when I was Amanda Diva, the host of Sucker Free Sunday on MTV2.

2
00:00:07,080 --> 00:00:09,960
Hey, welcome back. It's me and I'll be so sure.

3
00:00:10,420 --> 00:00:11,700
I gotta ask you something.

4
00:00:11,940 --> 00:00:12,360
What's up?

5
00:00:12,400 --> 00:00:14,220
Now, is that your real last name?

6
00:00:14,500 --> 00:00:15,760
No, but you know, everybody calls me.

7
00:00:15,760 --> 00:00:17,640
It's cool though. I like it. I like it.

8
00:00:17,640 --> 00:00:23,180
Thanks to their late manager, Rich Nichols, rest in peace, I hosted The Roots Picnic for several years.

9
00:00:23,860 --> 00:00:25,480
We're here at The Roots Picnic.

10
00:00:25,560 --> 00:00:29,000
Next up, we got J. Period and Black Thought Live mixtape and Mobb Deep.

11
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:30,160
It's performing!

12
00:00:31,040 --> 00:00:32,720
I DJed The Roots Picnic.

13
00:00:33,280 --> 00:00:36,840
I even painted at The Roots Picnic.

14
00:00:37,780 --> 00:00:43,500
I started my music journey around the same time Black Thought brought back the legendary Black Lily Festival.

15
00:00:43,500 --> 00:00:46,440
It had birthed voices like Jill Scott and Bahamidea.

16
00:00:46,880 --> 00:00:51,300
And as Amanda Diva, I was honored to now be in the lineage.

17
00:00:51,640 --> 00:00:55,140
And I got to perform my version of A Change Gonna Come.

18
00:00:55,480 --> 00:00:56,140
Are y'all ready?

19
00:00:56,200 --> 00:04:25,590
And the change is coming right now.

20
00:04:25,590 --> 00:04:30,430
Now it's 2026 and I'm reclaiming my timeline as Amanda Diva 2.0.

21
00:04:30,790 --> 00:04:33,590
My new album, Truth Translator, drops June 14th.

22
00:04:36,760 --> 00:04:37,880
It's not a movement.

23
00:04:38,380 --> 00:04:39,420
It's movement music.

